Week 3: Recursion, Searching & Linear Lists
1)Recursion Mechanics & Stack Frames: Understanding the execution call stack, tracking method stack frame allocation/
deallocation in Java's Stack memory, and preventing StackOverflowError.
2)Backtracking Algorithms: State space tree traversals, managing state changes, and recursion termination boundaries for
generating subsets, combinations, permutations, and string pattern matches.
3)Sorting Algorithms & Java Standards: Implementing Merge Sort and Quick Sort partitioning algorithms. Understanding
Java's built-in sorting mechanisms: Dual-Pivot Quicksort for primitive arrays (Arrays.sort()) and TimSort for object reference
arrays.
4)Binary Search Invariants: Standard binary search implementation, lower bound and upper bound index seeking, finding
first/last occurrences of elements, and searching within rotated sorted arrays.
5)Singly & Doubly Linked Lists: Constructing manual list nodes using reference objects. Pointer adjustments for node
insertion, unlinking, and deletion.
6)Linked List Algorithmic Patterns: In-place singly linked list reversal, merging two sorted lists, finding midpoints, and
Floyd’s Cycle Detection algorithm (Fast & Slow pointers).
